From 0b24757d16f9eb9853995023f4aad119e9050c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YoYoBatty <32651551+yoyobatty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:18:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Reuse job threads instead of starting one per job

Async jobs (http, sql, iconforge, unzip, sqlite) and fire-and-forget HTTP requests each started a new OS thread. They now run on a pool: a job goes to a waiting thread if there is one and gets a new thread if not, so a slow job never holds up the others. A thread with nothing to do for 60 seconds exits. A panicking job reports JOB PANICKED as before and the thread carries on.

Builds on the module pin: an idle pool thread wakes up to exit, which would crash in an unloaded rust_g.dll.
